#Problem APEX 2.4.34
## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Differentiation)
## DBsection(Derivatives of polynomials and power functions)
## KEYWORDS('derivative','horizontal tangent line')
## Institution(Valdosta State University)
## Author(S. V. Ault)
## Level(3)
## TitleText1('APEX Calculus')
## AuthorText1('Hartman')
## EditionText1('3.0')
## Section1('2.4')
## Problem1('34')

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

$a = random(2, 6) * random(-1, 1, 2);
$a2 = 2*$a;
$b = $a * non_zero_random(-5, 5);
$c = non_zero_random(-15, 15);

$ans = List(Real(-$b / (2 * $a)));

BEGIN_PGML
Let [`  f(x) = [$a] x^2 + [$b] x + [$c]  `].

Find all [`x`]-values where the graph of [`y=f(x)`] has a horizontal tangent line.  
Separate multiple [`x`]-values with commas.  
Enter *DNE* if there are no such [`x`].

[`x = `][_]{$ans}
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION

Set the derivative equal to zero.

[```
  \begin{aligned}
   f'(x) &= [$a2] x + [$b] \\
   [$a2] x + [$b] & = 0 \\
   x & = \frac{-[$b]}{[@ 2*$a@]} = [$ans]
  \end{aligned}
```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();

